WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.033
-Do you feel the love
out there?!

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.267
-I do!
[ Laughs ]

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.267
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.634
Please. Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.267
God, they love you. We love you.
-I love you.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.434
-Thanks for coming back
to the show.

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:13.734
-Yeah.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:14.734
-I didn't even know
if you were going to come back

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:15.834
after last time.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.834
-Yes.
-We did "Hot Ones" on the show.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.801
-That's right.
I was very upset with you.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.601
-Yeah, you were really --
-I was so mad.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.000
-The last time I saw you,
you were, like --

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.267
I think you were vomiting
in your dressing room.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.000
-Yes.
You came in like, "You good?"

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.067
I'm like, "No.
Get out of my room!"

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.701
-It was so funny.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.534
I told you backstage,
but I really mean this.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:34.033
I watched you during COVID.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.868
You did "Selena + Chef."

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:39.033
And, man, if you don't love
Selena Gomez in --

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.300
Like, if you can't love her
any more, watch this show.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.934
You were so charming
and cool and fun.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.167
I just loved it.
-Basically, I was an idiot.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.100
-No, no, you were so fun,
and I loved it.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.868
And I go, "Oh, that's just you
being fun and cool."

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.667
I just absolutely loved it.
I just wanted to say that.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.534
And then, I don't think I've
talked to you since

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:55.601
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:56.801
-Right.
-It's my favorite.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's the best show.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.133
-Yeah.
-It's the best show.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.634
-I had so much fun.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.868
Working with Steve and Marty --
it's honestly a dream.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:05.968
They're incredible.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.667
-Did you meet them before
you did the show?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.501
-No. I didn't.
-You just got cast in it.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.801
-Yeah. No, I actually met with
them before I got the part.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:12.934
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.400
-And are they
rubbing off on you?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.534
-Oh, completely.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.267
I've become
snarky and a little grumpy.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.000
Little grumpy.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.434
-No, they're just the best.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.701
-They are two of the funniest
human beings on Earth.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.934
And are you shooting Season 3?
-Yeah, we start in January.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:31.934
-You do? Alright, good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.968
I know -- You were
telling me backstage --

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.267
You were like, "Oh, yeah,
you do this thing."

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.133
And sometimes, I go,
"They just joke all the time."

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.534
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:41.200
And sometimes you go, "Yeah,
I'm going to roll by eyes."

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.767
-Oh, completely.
Are you kidding me?

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:45.000
I'm trained to roll my eyes
at both of them.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.868
They are so funny
and they just --

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.033
They'll tell the same jokes
every now and then.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.667
It's kind of like,
"Alright, guys."

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.200
-Yeah, but then -- Yeah.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.968
And then you just
said something,

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.400
and Marty Short
had a joke about Meryl Streep

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.868
and you got to meet
Meryl Streep.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.534
-Yeah, she came over
to the table.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.801
-So -- And you freaked out.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.234
I looked like
I was going to cry.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.601
-Yeah.
Because it's Meryl Streep.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:05.734
-It's Meryl Streep.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:06.901
-Yeah, she has that
effect on people.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.033
-Yeah, you think?
-Yeah, she does.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.868
But -- And you never met before?

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.400
-No. She grabbed my hand
and she kissed my hand.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.667
I was like, "Oh, my God!"

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.267
-We have a picture.
I wanted to show this.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.133
-Oh, God!
-She grabbed your hand here.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.133
And I go, "That's cool."
I had to show this.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.667
And then here's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.100
Yeah. Look at this.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.100
Come on!

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.133
-I'm so happy.
-I know you're so happy.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.701
-I'm so happy.
-How great is that?

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:32.033
-It was such
a surreal moment, honestly.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.501
You could only dream of,
you know,

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.033
meeting her
or working with her, you know?

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:38.534
-Yeah, exactly. She's a star.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:39.534
-Speaking of stars,
look at this.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:40.801
-Oh, God.
-Come on, look at this.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:46.267
Congrats.
-Thank you.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:47.767
-The cover of "Rolling Stone"?
Come on.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.000
-Thank you.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.767
-It's a great article,
by the way, in here.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:53.534
And what I liked
about it is, also,

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:56.334
your sense of humor comes
through in this article.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.901
But I know you
named your kidney.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.267
-Yes.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.934
-You named it
after someone we know.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.634
-Right. So, I got
a kidney transplant

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:07.067
a couple of years ago,
and as a way of coping,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.133
I thought I would name it.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.701
It's weird, I know, but I did.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.000
And I named it after
Fred Armisen.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.868
-Yeah, so Fred Armisen
is the name.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.300
Any -- Why?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.767
-Because I love "Portlandia"
and I love everything he does.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:22.167
And so I'm like, "Hey,
watch Fred, guys," you know?

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.400
-Fred Armisen.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.000
And does Fred Armisen
know that he --

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.901
-Yeah, he sent me flowers.
I was so excited.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.634
-Is that right? Did he really?

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:32.334
He's actually super-fun.
-Yeah, I heard he's awesome.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.000
-You should hang out with him.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.567
Can we talk about
"My Mind &amp; Me?"

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:39.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.767
The single is out now.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.167
And fans love it.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.234
And fans are all going on
the socials,

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.300
"Hey, does this mean there's
going to be more music?"

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.367
-Mm-hmm. That's accurate.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.000
-There is going to be more?
-Finally.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Finally.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.400
-I love that!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.534
-I'm just -- I'm so used to
writing sad-girl songs

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:00.601
because I'm good at that.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.567
But I'm ready to have some fun,

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.467
and I think people
are going to like it.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.434
-Oh, I can't wait.
Alright, good.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.968
So you're in the studio
now and working it?

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.968
-Yes. I'm actually doing
it here, which is awesome.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:13.300
-Oh, really?
It's all happening.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.734
Yeah, I know,
we're all part of it.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.701
I loved the documentary.
-Thank you.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:21.501
-And, man, oh, man,
I loved that you did it.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:24.367
I loved that you just kind of
let it all out there.

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.501
And when did you start
filming that?

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.167
-About six years ago --
seven years ago.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.434
-Seven years ago?
-Yeah.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:32.767
And we kind of went through
all the different phases

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.501
of my life from, you know,
getting diagnosed

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.868
and doing all the
things I had to go through.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.434
-Ooh! It's rough.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.300
-Yeah, it is.
I'm not going to lie.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.467
I can't watch it.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.567
And to be honest,
I was scared to release it.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:49.033
But I knew that being honest
and completely transparent was

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.501
what I want to be known for.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.567
I don't want to be
an unattainable thing.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:55.701
I want people to know that
it's not just you

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.000
and that they're not alone.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.934
-Yeah, that's exactly
what I took from it.

00:04:58.934 --> 00:04:59.934
Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.400
Thank you.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.968
-You do a lot for mental health,

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.634
and I know you actually visited
The White House.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:10.501
and met with the President
and the First Lady.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.400
-Yes.
And we discussed mental health.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.300
Now, I mean,
that was just a conversation.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.934
I hope that there's more
that's going to be happening.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.634
But it was really incredible to
be there with a bunch of

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.734
young people,
discussing mental health

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:24.767
and the crisis that we're in.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:28.534
-Not only the documentary
shows you performing

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:32.234
and writing songs and recording,
but it's like the touring

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.801
and also all
the charity work you do,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.267
it's just a lot for one human.

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:39.133
And that's what -- I mean,
it's a lot, what you do.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.367
-I know. I don't --
-Great things.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.467
-Yeah, I don't know how
I do it sometimes.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.734
I'm really tired.
-Yeah.

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:46.801
But it's amazing that you do.
And you give.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:51.200
And then, when, you do travel
to Africa and you go,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.334
"Hey, I feel great when
I do these things."

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:54.601
And that's another good message

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:55.934
I think people
can take from this, too.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.100
Like, when you do give
and do something for charity,

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.267
you feel good.

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:02.200
-Completely.
I feel like I have a purpose.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.234
And, in some ways,
I feel selfish

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:05.767
because I want to do more.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:09.367
But I do know that I won't stop
this fight until the day I die.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.634
I think mental health
is incredibly important

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.634
and should be focused on.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:17.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.767
-My favorite part --
Also, by the way, I'm in it.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:24.133
My voice is in --
-I know.

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:25.434
-That's not my favorite part.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:28.767
My favorite part is
when you go to your hometown,

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:29.934
where you grew up,

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:31.734
and you go to your house
where you were raised.

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.400
-Yes.
-And you have the home videos.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.133
And you're still so cute.
-Oh, thanks.

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:37.167
-But you go to your home
and you're like,

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:38.868
"Oh, I remember this and that."

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.400
And it's changed.
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.234
-But then you go,
"Hey, I think I wrote on

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.968
the back of this --"
Is it a door or a wall?

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:46.634
-Yes, I did. It was a mirror.
-It's a mirror.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:49.467
And he actually still has it.
-Yes, he does.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:55.567
-And you wrote,
"Cole Sprouse" with a heart.

00:06:55.567 --> 00:06:58.667
Did you have a crush on
Cole Sprouse?

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:00.400
-Yes, I did.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.601
And my first kiss
was his brother.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:07.234
-What?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:10.601
What?! Dylan?
-On TV. On TV.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:13.868
-Oh, it's --
You kissed the wrong Sprouse?

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:15.701
-They wrote it
in the script that way.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.534
-Oh, okay. It was part of the --
-It was the show, yes.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:18.601
-Oh, "Suite Life
of Zack &amp; Cody."

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:20.534
-Yes.
-Okay, so, you went on there.

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.667
But why didn't you do
the scene with Cole?

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:25.000
Were you bummed, secretly?
-Oh, I can't say that.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.534
That isn't what it was.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:29.300
I think I felt much better
that it wasn't him,

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.434
because I think I would
have probably been an idiot.

00:07:32.434 --> 00:07:35.200
-He was the love of your life.
-He was the love of my life.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.467
-He was the crush.
-He was.

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:40.167
-I want to read some reviews on
the documentary, by the way,

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:41.801
if you want to plug your ears.

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.501
-Yeah, just a little bit.
-Yeah.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.701
-"Sincere and soul-bearing,"
"New York Times."

00:07:45.701 --> 00:07:49.467
"Selena Gomez: My Mind &amp; Me"
explains much about the star,

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:52.067
the culture, and movement,"
"Wall Street Journal."

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:54.133
"Rolling Stone" said
"profound and powerful."

00:07:54.133 --> 00:07:56.667
And it's 97% fresh on
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:58.100
It's a hit, bud.
-Thank you.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.734
-It's cool that you did it.

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:01.400
It's really good
that you did it.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.501
For everyone out there,
check it out.

00:08:02.501 --> 00:08:03.934
Please take a look.

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:06.467
Here's Selena's new documentary,
"Selena Gomez: My Mind &amp; Me."

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:07.601
Check this out.

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:08.901
-When I first got out,

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:12.567
I didn't know how
I'd cope with my diagnosis.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.634
What if it happened again?

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:18.400
What if the next time,
I didn't come back?

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.133
I needed to keep
learning about it.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.834
I needed to take it day by day.

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:28.601
When I was a kid, I was
terrified of thunderstorms.

00:08:28.601 --> 00:08:31.300
I grew up in Texas
and I was so scared that

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.634
lightning and thunder
would mean a tornado was coming.

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:36.901
But my mom gave me
these books for kids

00:08:36.901 --> 00:08:39.634
that explained storms
and lightning and thunder

00:08:39.634 --> 00:08:42.601
and basically said,
"The more you learn about it,

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:44.033
the less you're going to be
afraid of it."

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:46.400
And it really helped.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.567
-Selena Gomez, everyone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.567 --> 00:08:53.367
"Selena Gomez: My Mind &amp; Me"
is streaming now on Apple TV+.

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:55.634
Sebastian Maniscalco
joins us next.

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:56.634
Stick around, everybody.

